<<<
significant point is that, in II of shade, shadow is offered as a definition of shade, without reciprocity in II of shadow, the inference from which is that in division IL shadow is the normal word, & shade exceptional.
===
significant point is that, in II of *shade*, *shadow* is offered as a definition of *shade*, without reciprocity in II of *shadow*, the inference from which is that in division II *shadow* is the normal word, & *shade* exceptional.
>>>

<<<
So too we say light & shade but lights & shadows, in the shade but under a shadow; & so too shady means full of shade, but shadowy like a shadow.
===
So too we say *light & shade* but *lights & shadows*, *in the shade* but *under a shadow*; & so too *shady* means full of shade, but *shadowy* like a shadow.
>>>

